# Fleet standard. text=auto normalizes the index to LF; eol=lf pins the WORKING TREE to LF too.
#
# Why eol=lf and not bare text=auto: with core.autocrlf=true the checkout-canonical form is CRLF,
# but every agent tool (Edit, WriteAllText, the generators) writes LF. Git cannot see the difference
# (CRLF->LF on the way in collapses both), so files silently drift into MIXED endings inside a
# single file - invisible to `git status`, and already the cause of byte-exact-compare ghost bugs
# (2026-08-28 kernel triage) and a generator emitting mixed output (2026-08-29, checklist skills).
# Pinning eol=lf makes the canonical form equal what the tools produce, so the drift cannot recur.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the one real exception: cmd.exe can mis-parse LF-terminated labels/goto.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf